## Ingestion Script Plan (seed_kb.py)

### Location
`backend/scripts/seed_kb.py`

### How it works
1. Import `ingest_document` from `app.services.chat_rag` directly (bypasses HTTP/auth).
2. Import `get_supabase_client` or create a Supabase client using service role key.
3. Define a list of documents as Python dicts: `source_key`, `title`, `category`, `content`.
4. Loop through documents and call `ingest_document(...)` for each.
5. Print chunk count per document as confirmation.

### Documents to seed (minimum for demo)
| source_key | title | category |
|---|---|---|
| `tw-faq-bookings` | TourWise Booking FAQ | faq |
| `tw-faq-external` | External Partner Trips FAQ | faq |
| `tw-policy-cancellation` | Cancellation & Refund Policy | policy |
| `tw-guide-platform` | Platform Overview & How To Use | guide |

### Environment
- Script reads `.env` from `backend/` (same as main app).
- Requires `GOOGLE_API_KEY` / `GEMINI_API_KEY` and `SUPABASE_*` vars to be set.
- Run from workspace root: `python backend/scripts/seed_kb.py`

### Safety
- `ingest_document` uses upsert on `source_key` — safe to re-run without duplicates.
- Old chunks for a document are deleted and replaced on each run.
- Script is idempotent.
